<title>FRANCE: JAN-FEB 97 POSTAL TRAFFIC DECREASES - ADP.</title>
<headline>JAN-FEB 97 POSTAL TRAFFIC DECREASES - ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle (CDG) and Orly, handled 22,777 tonnes of postal traffic in January-February 1997, an decrease of 1.4 percent on the same period the previous year, Paris airport authority (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The number of flights  wholly dedicated to postal traffic totalled 1,424 an increase of 11.4 percent on January-February 1996. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
